==Trivia==
* Eagle was reworked into its current version in [[Updates/26|Update 26]]. Before its rework, Eagle was known as [[Falcon]].
* A physical Eagle Fruit can be obtained from defeating the [[Tyrant of the Skies]].
* The {{Skin|Parrot}} and {{Skin|Falcon}} skins depict another species of bird, rather than variations of eagles.
* The sound effects of the {{Ability|F}} move are similar to awakened [[Phoenix]]'s {{Ability|Phoenix|V}} move, as both make the scream of a {{w|Red-tailed hawk}}.
* Eagle's physical fruit model is noticeably small when compared to other fruit models.
* A real life bald eagle typically cruise at around 13.5 meters per second, and soar at speeds up to 45 meters per second. The in-game counterpart, however, flies at around 10 meters per second, and approximately 40-44 meters per second when lunging forwards with {{Ability|V}} or upgraded {{Ability|F}}.
* The game considers Eagle's {{Ability|F}} a transformation which needs to be disabled in order to change fruits or use the [[Portals|Portal]] in [[Tiki Outpost]]. 
* After [[Updates/30|Update 30]], [[Eagle|Eagle's]] [F] Flight move is actually faster than awakened [[Light|Light's]] [F] move, making it one of the fastest flights in the game. 

* The {{CHROMATIC}} skins also have some trivia:
** {{Skin|Matrix}}'s color scheme seems to be inspired by the green and black of a computer hacker's coding screen. It bears a strong resemblance to the colours of the [https://roblox-elemental-battlegrounds.fandom.com/wiki/Technology Technology] element from [https://roblox-elemental-battlegrounds.fandom.com/wiki/Roblox_Elemental_Battlegrounds_Wiki Elemental Battlegrounds], another game developed by [[Gamer Robot Inc|Gamer Robot]].
** {{Skin|Parrot}}'s color scheme is based off the {{w|Scarlet Macaw}}, one of the most iconic species of parrot.

